     "**Color Mapping:** Map `max_val` to a color.",
     "*   **Step Size:** Determines sampling density.",
     "Prevents hole formation in non-axial views caused by undersampling by applying a morphological closing operation (e.g., 2x2x2 structuring element) to the final 2D projection image.",
     "A local projection technique for vascular diagnosis that selects the first local maximum above a dataset-specific threshold.",
     "Approximates MIP using Fourier Volume Rendering by transforming voxel values $v \\to b^v$ (e.g., $b=2$ or $1.1$), performing FVR projection, and applying a base-$b$ logarithm.",
     "Suffers from artifacts due to non-linear compression of resampling filters.",
     "An importance compositing method where for each ray, only the object with the highest importance is displayed densely; all remaining objects are fully transparent.",
     "Uses depth buffer clipping and gradient modification to enhance focus objects.",
     "Maps voxel intensity to screen depth to resolve occlusion in dense volumes, ensuring highly conserved (high intensity) regions are displayed before less conserved ones using a Z-buffer algorithm."
